  "brief": "Pioneer-era 1.5-storey hewn-log cabin with dovetailed corners and chinked joints, weathered silver-grey: a steep side-gabled wood-shingle roof sweeping down over a full-width front porch on rough posts with knee braces and a plank floor. Small six-light windows, a plank door with a house-number post, a vertical-board lean-to shed at one end. Preserved as the town's founding-era relic amid tulip beds and a flowering crabapple.",
